     "result_text_tail": "g in Pro still adds about $2.4M of net ARR in year one. The deck ends with five launch conditions and five next steps, each with an owner and a date.\n\n**Choices I made for you:**\n- **Audience:** the CEO and executive team, approving the launch and its packaging and price at January 2027 planning.\n- **Storyline:** I approved it myself rather than stopping for your review.\n- **Usage limit:** I set it at 667 AI requests per seat per month, the level where model costs take half of the $12 seat premium. It is the one number in the deck that isn't from the briefing pack. It's labelled as my working assumption in the sources workbook.\n- **Usage cost:** I counted the $0.6M a year of platform cost against gross margin, which is the cautious reading.\n\nAll 99 numbers come from the briefing pack or are calculated from it, and no \"?\" placeholders are left. Figures like the $2.9M and $2.4M are my estimates. Each shows its calculation on the slide and has a live formula in the workbook. One QA warning remains, and it's harmless: the pack writes the mobile delay as \"two quarters\" in words, so the checker can't match it to a figure. There were no web sources, so I didn't run the source re-check.\n\nIf you'd like, I can switch the theme, or test what happens if fewer accounts move to Pro than the 2023 tier's 33%.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- brightwork-copilot.pptx\n- brightwork-copilot-sources.xlsx\n\nThe spec and its build script are in `./work/` if you want to change and re-render the deck."
